---
title: "reserve::borrow_flash_loan / repay_flash_loan (Current Finance: Lending Protocol)"
---
stateDiagram-v2
    direction TB
    [*] --> q_borrow_check: amount < cash?
    q_borrow_check --> q_error_cash: amount >= cash
    q_borrow_check --> q_withdraw: amount < cash
    q_error_cash --> [*]: abort reserve_flash_loan_more_than_cash
    q_withdraw --> q_create_potato: flash_loan_withdraw(amount)
    q_create_potato --> q_return: ReserveFlashLoan { amount }
    q_return --> q_repay_check: ... (user executes arbitrage) ...
    q_repay_check --> q_check_repay_amount: repay_flash_loan called
    q_check_repay_amount --> q_error_repay: coin.value() != loan.amount
    q_check_repay_amount --> q_join: coin.value() == loan.amount
    q_error_repay --> [*]: abort reserve_flash_loan_not_paid_enough
    q_join --> q_check_fee: underlying_balance.join(coin)
    q_check_fee --> q_zero_fee: fee.value() == 0
    q_check_fee --> q_add_fee: fee.value() > 0
    q_zero_fee --> [*]: fee.destroy_zero()
    q_add_fee --> [*]: cash_reserve += fee, cash += fee

    note right of q_withdraw
        INV-001: flash loan does NOT deduct from cash counter (only from balance)
        INV-002: flash loan does NOT affect debt tracking
        INV-003: fee goes entirely to cash_reserve (protocol revenue)
        INV-004: reserves allowed to be borrowed via flash loan
        INV-005: ReserveFlashLoan is consumed (hot potato pattern)
    end note
